                                                                                                                <comments>
                            <comment id="16332222" author="ptupitsyn" created="Fri, 19 Jan 2018 13:01:57 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Looks like there is no way to fix this issue in code. Core CLR attempts to load that assembly right at the start, not lazily. No code is executed before that.&lt;br/&gt;
See &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/dotnet/standard/issues/506&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/dotnet/standard/issues/506&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16347088" author="ptupitsyn" created="Wed, 31 Jan 2018 16:23:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Reopening. Turns out it worked in nightly builds right after &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2662&quot; title=&quot;.NET Core support (run on Linux)&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-2662&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-2662&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; was merged, and was broken after &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-6615&quot; title=&quot;.NET: Thin client: XML configuration&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-6615&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-6615&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; merge.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Looks like this is caused by generic &lt;tt&gt;GetConfigurationSection&amp;lt;T&amp;gt;&lt;/tt&gt; method, may be removing generic constraint will fix the problem?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16347163" author="ptupitsyn" created="Wed, 31 Jan 2018 16:50:43 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;Weakening generic constraint to &lt;tt&gt;class&lt;/tt&gt; fixed the issue.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Merged to master: &lt;tt&gt;0088405ce305a915174c53bcafcc9a1740da64c7&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;br/&gt;
Cherry-picked to ignite-2.4: &lt;tt&gt;aca3b8c664de8dcbbfeabbb0f8c252194d6ad1b2&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
